      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The source draws the right triangle. √ x2 + 9, so For x &gt; 0, its hypotenuse is p x2 + 9)(x/ p x2 + 9). 2 sin θ cos θ = 2(3/ For x &lt; 0 the sine changes sign, giving the same rational expression: Equating to 6x/25 and cancelling 6x gives 9 + x2 = 25. Since x̸ = 0, x2 = 16. [A1] For x = ±4, | tan θ| = 3/4 &lt; 1, [A1] hence |2θ| &lt; π/2. [A1] Sine is one-to-one on the principal range, so both candidates solve the original equation: x = ±4 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:670.7px\"></figure>",
