    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"( ) 2 x , x∈ . f x ≡ 4e − 28 a) Sketch the graph of f x . ( ) The sketch must include the coordinates of any intersections with the coordinate axes and the equations of any asymptotes. ( ) 3 The equation f x ( ) − 40 = 3 x has a negative root α . b) Show that α = − 4.00045 , correct to 5 decimal places. ( ) 5 ( ) The equation f x − 40 = 3 x also has a positive root β .\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q4-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) Use a numerical method, based on an iterative method, to determine the value of β correct to 5 decimal places. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:593.5px\"></figure>",
