    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q5-question-1.svg\" alt=\"In the convergent expansion of n ( 1 + kx ) , kx &lt; , 1 2 where k and n are non zero constants, the coefficient of x is 12 and the coefficient 3 x is 32. of Given the coefficient of x is negative determine the values of k and n . ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q5-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Write the binomial expansion through the cubic term: (1 + kx)n = 1 + nkx + 1 2n(n −1)k2x2 + 1 6n(n −1)(n −2)k3x3 + O(x4) 1 2n(n −1)k2 = 12 1 6n(n −1)(n −2)k3 = 32 The coefficients give n(n −1)k2 = 24 [B1] and n(n −1)(n −2)k3 = 192. [A1] Division gives k(n −2) = 8. [A1] Substitute k = 8/(n −2) [M1] into the first relation and clear the denominator: 2  8 n(n −1) = 24 n −2 64n(n −1) = 24 (n −2)2 64n2 −64n = 24(n −2)2\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"64n2 −64n = 24(n2 −4n + 4) 64n2 −64n = 24n2 −96n + 96 40n2 + 32n −96 = 0 5n2 + 4n −12 = 0 This gives 5n2 + 4n −12 = (5n −6)(n + 2) . [A1] = 0 The pairs (k, n) are (−10, 6/5) and (−2, −2). [A1] The linear coefficient nk &lt; 0 [A1] excludes nk = (−2)(−2) = 4, and nk = (6/5)(−10) = −12 selects k = −10, n = 6/5 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 5 is 8 marks.</p>"
