      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q6-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The three centres form an equilateral triangle of side 12. [M1] Each common external tangent segment has the same length as the corresponding side: [A1] At each cylinder the straight portions turn by the exterior angle 120◦, so the three radius-6 arcs have total angle 2π. [A1] At one centre the angle is 2π −2(π/2) −π/3 = 2π/3; its arc length is 6(2π/3) = 4π. Three copies of a straight section and an arc therefore give 3(12 + 4π). The band length is 3(12) + 6(2π) = 12(π + 3) cm . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 6 is 4 marks.</p>"
    ],
