    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-v/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"2 2 Mould is spreading on a wall of area 20 m and when it was first noticed 2 m of the wall was already covered by this mould. 2 Let A , in m , represent the area of the wall covered by the mould, after time t weeks. The rate at which A is changing is proportional to the product of the area covered by the mould and the area of the wall not yet covered by the mould. 2 After a further period of 2 weeks the area of the wall covered by the mould is 4 m . By forming and solving a suitable differential equation, show that 20 ( ) A = . 12 t ( ) 2 1 9 3 +\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q11-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:589.5px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Set dA/dt = kA(20 −A) [M1] [A1] with k &gt; 0. [A1] Separate and use 1/[A(20 −A)] = 1 20[1/A + 1/(20 −A)]. [M1] Clear denominators in P/A + Q/(20 −A) to get 1 = P(20 −A) + QA. Substituting 0 and 20 gives P = Q = 1/20. Multiply the separated equation by 20 and integrate: ln A −ln |20 −A| = 20kt + C. Integration gives ln[A/(20 −A)] = 20kt + C. [M1] At t = 0, A = 2, [A1] so A/(20 −A) = e20kt/9. [A1] At t = 2, A = 4 [A1] gives e40k = 9/4, [A1] hence e20k = 3/2. [A1] Write a = 20k = ln(3/2), then rearrange: 9A 20 −A = eαt\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"9A 20 −A = e(ln 3 2 )t 9A 3 t 20 −A = 2 3 t (20 −A) = 9A 2 t t 3 3 −A = 9A 20 2 2 t t 3 3 20 = 9A + A 2 2 &quot; 3 t# 3 t A 9 + = 20 2 2 t  3 20 2 A = t + 9  3 2\" style=\"--madas-width:421.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-v/q11-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Divide by (3/2)t. Solving for A yields 20 A = 1 + 9(2/3)t . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
